instrument wingie
; wingie-proc-dub-time — line in through the dub mixer, a tape loop, Pauline Oliveros' delays and
; a PT2399 with a Coco behind it: time bent, thrown, looped and worn. Set the Line/Mic switch to line.
;
; every scene:
;   fader1 (Mix)     the time: echo length, loop speed, how fast the delays wander
;   fader2 (Decay)   the feedback: how long things come round (past the top: careful)
;   fader3 (Volume)  the tone or the wear inside the loop
;   mode1            held: throw the line into the echo / punch it onto the tape / hold it
;   keys             filter sweeps, pitch for the heads, strikes; octave1 an octave on the keys
;   left LED         the line in;  right LED  what comes round
; Step through the scenes with a held Mode button and a tap on the other.

the siren in the yard
---------------------
; a dub send: only while mode1 (or any bottom key) is held does the line go into the echo, with
; its spring splash and a tone inside the loop. The echo runs through a band filter the bottom
; keys place (C low, B high) and out across a ping-pong; hold mode2 and an LFO sweeps it. When
; you play, the echoes duck under you and swell back when you stop.
the send is dub
the sweep is svf 8 res=0.6
the wobble is lfo rate=0.3
the wobbler is vca
the ear is follower attack=0.01 release=0.35
the duck is ducker
the bounce is pingpong 4 time=0.75 feedback=0.3
the guardl is limiter ceiling=0.9
the guardr is limiter ceiling=0.9

line.both -> send ear
mode1 keys1.gate -> send.throw
fader1 -> send.time
fader2 -> send.feedback
fader3 -> send.tone
send.wet -> sweep
keys1.key -> sweep.cutoff
wobble.sine -> wobbler
mode2 => wobbler.gain
wobbler -50> sweep.cutoff
sweep.band -> duck
ear -> duck.side
duck -> bounce
send.out bounce.l -> guardl
send.out bounce.r -> guardr
bounce.l -15> send               ; the ping-pong back into the send
guardl -> left
guardr -> right
ear -> lights.left
send.wet -> lights.right

frippertronics
--------------
; a six-second tape loop: hold mode1 and the line in is recorded over it (some of the old
; stays); let go and it goes round, wearing as it goes (fader3 how fast it ages). The bottom
; keys play the tape at their pitch (C as recorded), octave1 an octave slower or faster. A tap
; on mode2 throws the second head into a ping-pong. fader1 how much of the loop, fader2 how
; much of the ping-pong comes back round onto the tape.
the loop is tapeloop seconds=6 gap=0.37
the oct1 is transpose
the second is vca
the latch is flipflop
the bounce is pingpong 3 time=0.6 feedback=0.4
the blur is diffuser
the wide is widener width=0.8
the mix is vca

line.both -> loop
mode1 -> loop.punch
fader3 -> loop.age
octave1 -> oct1
keys1.pitch -> oct1.pitch
oct1 -> loop.speed
loop.right -> second
mode2.tap -> latch
latch => second.gain
second -> bounce
bounce.l bounce.r -> blur
fader2 -> blur.amount
blur -30> loop                    ; the ping-pong onto the tape
loop.left -> mix
fader1 -> mix.gain
mix -> wide
loop.right -60> wide.right
wide.left bounce.l -> left
wide.right bounce.r -> right
line.both -40> out
mode1 -> lights.left
loop.left -> lights.right

the expanded instrument
-----------------------
; four delays whose times wander, feeding each other and turning around the room (after Pauline
; Oliveros' EIS), fed by a granular delay that sings back pitched to the bottom keys: an
; octave up and fed back it climbs like a shimmer. fader1 how fast the four wander, fader2 how
; far, fader3 the feedback among them. The louder you play the more the grains scatter. Hold
; mode1 and the grains feed back on themselves; a top key held freezes the wandering.
the eis is eis samplerate=half
the glass is graindelay 2 samplerate=half time=0.5 density=0.5
the ear is follower attack=0.01 release=0.6
the oct1 is transpose
the hold is crossfade
the guardl is limiter ceiling=0.9
the guardr is limiter ceiling=0.9

line.both -> glass ear
octave1 -> oct1
keys1.pitch -> oct1.pitch
oct1 -> glass.pitch
ear -60> glass.jitter
mode1 -50> glass.feedback
glass.left glass.right -> eis
line.both -40> eis
fader1 -> hold.a
keys2.gate -> hold.mix
hold -> eis.rate                  ; fader1, or nothing while a top key is held
fader2 -> eis.depth
fader3 -> eis.feedback
eis.left glass.left -> guardl
eis.right glass.right -> guardr
guardl -> left
guardr -> right
ear -> lights.left
eis.left -> lights.right

the chip and the coco
---------------------
; a PT2399 echo (turn fader1 and the pitch bends), then a Chloe tube and filter, then a Coco:
; an 8-bit delay whose clock is its time. Every attack in the line in strikes the Chloe's gate;
; the top keys place its filter. mode1 freezes the Coco's loop, a tap on mode2 flips it backwards,
; any bottom key makes its head skip. fader2 the chip's feedback, fader3 the Coco's.
the chip is pt2399
the valve is chloe mode=band drive=0.4 resonance=0.5
the ear is follower attack=0.002 release=0.12
the hit is trigger length=20
the coco is coco 1 rate=0.6
the latch is flipflop
the guard is limiter ceiling=0.9

line.both -> chip ear
ear.gate -> hit
fader1 -> chip.time
fader2 -80> chip.feedback         ; never quite into the scream
chip -> valve
hit -> valve.gate
keys2.key -> valve.cutoff
valve -> coco
mode1 -> coco.freeze
mode2.tap -> latch
latch -> coco.flip
keys1.trig -> coco.skip
fader3 -> coco.feedback
chip -60> guard
valve -40> guard
coco.verso -> left
coco.inverso -> right
guard -> out
ear -> lights.left
coco -> lights.right
